WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.530
WiTrack is a new technology
that performs 3D motion tracking

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:08.970
of a person purely using
radio reflections of her body,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:12.660
even if the person is moving
behind a wall or furniture.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:15.210
WiTrack is placed behind
the wall of this room,

00:00:15.210 --> 00:00:17.700
as indicated by the red arrow.

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.680
As the person walks
around in the room,

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.840
it tracks his motion
through the wall.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:24.810
In the adjacent room,
WiTrack outputs the location

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.690
of the person as a
red dot on the screen.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.180
As the person moves
around behind the wall,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.600
the red dot moves on the screen,
indicating his exact location

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.530
at any point in time.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:37.950
So let us see how WiTrack works.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.290
WiTrack performs
3D motion tracking

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.930
using body radio reflections.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.060
It transmits wireless
signals whose power

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.880
is 100 times less than
Wi-Fi and 1,000 times

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.190
smaller than cell
phone transmissions.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.260
These signals will
reflect off the person

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.300
and come back to its receive
antennas after some delay.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.300
WiTrack measures the
delays and maps them

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.610
to the distance
traveled by the signals.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.040
Based on a geometric
model of the antennas,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.690
WiTrack can now
accurately determine

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.400
the location of the person.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.680
The model incorporates
new algorithms

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.200
that remove reflections
due to walls and furniture

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.960
and focus only on the
reflections of a human body,

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:14.880
even if the person
is behind a wall

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.890
or in a completely
different room.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.760
In this demo the person walks
on a spiral on the ground

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.140
as the red dot tracks him
in the bottom left corner

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:23.753
of the screen.

00:01:23.753 --> 00:01:25.170
Note that the
spiral on the ground

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:27.720
is only there to show the
accuracy of the system

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.150
and is not used to aid
localization in any way.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:33.920
This system has a large
number of applications.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.420
For example, it performs highly
accurate localization simply

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.520
using reflections
off a person's body

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:43.030
without requiring the
person to hold any device.

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:46.000
It can also be used in gaming,
where it can start players

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.180
as they run down hallways or
hide behind furniture and walls

00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:51.130
for video game enemies.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.960
The system not only tracks
the location of a person,

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:56.470
but it can also
track his body parts.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.140
In this example, the person is
controlling different household

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:02.020
appliances, turning them
on and off by simply

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:05.570
pointing his hand
in their direction.

00:02:05.570 --> 00:02:07.490
Because WiTrack
works through walls,

00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.710
it can allow you to
control appliances even

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.110
from another room.

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:14.360
So you leave a room and
forget to turn off the lights.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.190
All you have to do
is point your hand

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.610
in the direction of that
room to turn the lights off.

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.820
WiTrack therefore can perform
3D motion tracking of humans

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:25.370
and body parts simply
using radio reflections

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.830
off a person's body.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:30.130
And it works even through
walls and obstructions.

